a and the helots of Messenia revolt</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">404 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> surrenders to Sparta, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">371 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece">Thebes</a> defeats Sparta at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuctra">Battle of Leuctra</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">222 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleomenes-iii">Cleomenes III</a> is defeated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sellasia">Battle of Sellasia</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">146 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaean-war">Achaean War</a> Sparta becomes a free city allied to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a></span></li></ol>
